<title>HUNGARY: Hungary trade gap down to $1.9 bln in Jan-Sept.</title>
<headline>Hungary trade gap down to $1.9 bln in Jan-Sept.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungary's January-September trade deficit narrowed to $1.935 billion according to preliminary figures from $2.03 billion in the January-September period of 1995, the National Bank of Hungary said in a statement on Friday.</p>
<p>The trade deficit was down at $173 million in September from $324 million in August and compared to a deficit of $95 million in September 1995, it said.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom (36 1) 327-4040</p>
